1)Identify the aspects of your application that vary and seperate them from what stays the same
2)Program to an interface, not an implementation
3)Favor composition over inheritance


| Rank | Pattern              | Type                | Common use case                                    |
| ---- | -------------------- | ------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |
| 1    | Dependency Injection | Architectural / IoC | Inject services into Angular components            |
| 2    | Factory Method       | Creational          | Create objects based on a type                     |
| 3    | Strategy             | Behavioral          | Switch payment, sorting, or validation algorithms  |
| 4    | Observer             | Behavioral          | Events, RxJS, reactive data                        |
| 5    | Singleton            | Creational          | One shared instance of a service                   |
| 6    | Adapter              | Structural          | Integrate third-party APIs with your code          |
| 7    | Decorator            | Structural          | Add behavior without modifying the original class  |
| 8    | Facade               | Structural          | Provide a simple interface over complex operations |
| 9    | Proxy                | Structural          | Control access, caching, or lazy loading           |
| 10   | Builder              | Creational          | Construct complex objects step by step             |
| 11   | State                | Behavioral          | Change behavior according to the current state     |
| 12   | Command              | Behavioral          | Encapsulate an action as an object                 |
